Tokens, wall time, USD, and acts are descriptive for capability. They cannot veto a capability pass or rescue a failed capability claim. The ITT token ratio is descriptive; only the paired-success token ratio enters the efficiency-only conjunction.

## Forced interpretation

`capability_pass` requires the one-sided 95% lower bound for C minus B ITT success to exceed zero. `efficiency_only` is available only when capability does not pass and every precommitted success, paired-token, dead-end, and timeout/cap condition holds. It supports only an efficiency product, not a capability claim. Component isolations can remove or replace a component but cannot create a headline pass.

Gate 1A, validation, and held-out status are controlled by the artifact-freeze manifest and independent review records. This report does not open a gate.
